.TH BUNKER 1 "July 2026" "nixos-bunker" "NixOS-bunker Manual"
.SH NAME
bunker \- hardened microVM workstation operator UI and tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bunker
.br
.B bunker-zone
.RI [ list | add | set | rm | ... ]
.br
.B bunker-zone-start
.IR zone
.br
.B bunker-term
.IR zone
.br
.B bunker-clip
.RI [ send | copy ]
.IR ...
.br
.B bunker-file
copy
.IR srcZone:/path
.IR dstZone:/path
.br
.B bunker-wipe
.IR zone
.br
.B bunker-host-net
.RI [ allow | lock | status ]
.br
.B bunker-sflc
.RI [ bootstrap | unlock | lock | status ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Thin GNOME host. Daily apps run in microVM
.BR zones .
Brokers:
.B net
(SOCKS: Nym / I2P / Tor / Tor-over-Nym) and
.B usb
(usbip, one device to one zone).
.P
Primary UI:
.B bunker
(ratatui TUI). Policy lives in
.IR config/zones.json
(public) and Shufflecake
.I hidden-zones.json
(deniable).
.SH TUI KEYS
.TS
l l.
s	start net / usb / zone / all
e	terminal into selected zone (new window → bunker-term)
v	USB attach/detach for selected zone
h	host clearnet allow / lock / status
b	Shufflecake bootstrap
a / d / r	add / delete / rename zone
c / t / n	color / kind / internet backend
i / u	hide (deniable) / unlock layer
o	ISO path for zone
f	mediated file copy
Space	cycle panic keep|lock|wipe
p	arm panic
w	save
?	help
q	quit
.TE
.SH INTERNET BACKENDS
Set per zone (TUI
.BR n
or
.BR "bunker-zone set … internet=" ).
.TS
l l.
nym	SOCKS → Nym mixnet
i2p	SOCKS → i2pd
tor	SOCKS → Tor (direct)
nym-tor	cascade: Tor-over-Nym
i2p-tor	cascade: Tor-over-I2P
tor-nym	cascade: Nym-over-Tor
i2p-nym	cascade: Nym-over-I2P
none	air-gap style (LAN only, no WAN SOCKS)
.TE
.P
Cascade names are
.BR inner-outer
(guest speaks to outer). I2P-as-outer cascades (nym-i2p / tor-i2p) are
.B not
supported — see
.IR docs/egress.md .
No 3+ hop chains.
.SH NOT IN THE TUI
Use CLI / rebuild as below (TUI can still
.B h
allow/lock around rebuilds).
.TS
l l.
nixos-rebuild	terminal after TUI h→allow; then h→lock
clipboard	bunker-clip send|copy
manual disposable wipe	bunker-wipe ZONE (or panic wipe)
edit apps[] / mem / diskGb	bunker-zone set … / edit JSON; then rebuild
per-app “open in qube” menu	GNOME zone launchers start the VM; run apps inside
.TE
.SH DENIABLE ZONES
Hidden friendly names are
.B not
in public
.IR zones.json .
Unlock (TUI
.BR u )
merges
.I layerN/hidden-zones.json
and maps names to anonymous slots
.BR d1..dN .
See
.IR docs/deniable.md .
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR docs/USER-GUIDE.md ,
